<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khải Định</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a>–<a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Khai Dinh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khải Định was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Nguyen dynasty from 1916 to 1925, under the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. Placed on the throne after the exile of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duy-tan">Duy Tân</a>, he cooperated closely with the colonial authorities and visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1922, drawing criticism from nationalists such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phan-chau-trinh">Phan Châu Trinh</a>. His elaborate tomb near Huế combines Vietnamese and European styles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khai-dinh.jpg" alt="Khải Định" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: H. Manuel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kh%E1%BA%A3i_%C4%90%E1%BB%8Bnh,_empereur_d%27Annam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
